$grp PS_MissionDescription : "{3136BE42592F3B1B}PrefabsEditable/MissionDescription/EditableMissionDescription.et" {
 D1_Situation {
  m_sTitle "Situation"
  m_sTextData "<h2>I. SITUATION</h2>"\
  ""\
  "<b>a. Enemy Forces</b>"\
  ""\
  "While most enemy forces have retreated to the north east, a limited presence of enemies is expected within the forest to the east."\
  ""\
  "Preliminary intel suggests they are distributed into small teams, and tasked with delaying movement of US forces through the forest, largely by setting up obstacles along roads and to a more limited extent, conducting ambushes."\
  ""\
  "They are largely using Soviet-style small arms. While they likely posess only few portable AT weapons, the enemy was observed making effective use of heavy machine guns in some previous encounters, which can pose a serious threat to LAVs. Armed vehicles are not expected in significant numbers."\
  ""\
  "For obstacles, the enemy may e. g. use AT mines, razor wire, abatises or vehicle barricades."\
  ""\
  "<b>b. Friendly Forces</b>"\
  ""\
  "One light armored reconaissance platoon, currently located outside of Kamoryn, preparing for a route reconnaissance mission."
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 1
 }
 D3_Notes {
  coords 0 0 0
  m_sTitle "Notes"
  m_sTextData "End conditions:"\
  "- Major Victory: 70% of alive US forces reach the western end of the AO, after fully clearing an uninterrupted road towards it of obstacles and enemies"\
  "- Minor Victory: Same as above but without 100% clearing a route"\
  "- Defeat: Reached 70% casualties or 50m minute time limit"\
  ""\
  ""\
  "Route validity:"\
  "- The cleared route must be fully uninterrupted, i. e. if it's required to move offroad then that is not considered viable - it must be an actual connected road on the map. There are no other limitations in regard to this."\
  "- There cannot be any remaining obstacles on the cleared route, or enemies in the immediate vicinity (destroying enemies that are further away is not required). Some major obstacles cannot be removed, in that case an alternative route must be found."\
  "- Obstacle placement is randomized."\
  "- It is encouraged that PL/PSG mark cleared segments of the road or major obstacles on the map to avoid confusion."\
  ""\
  "AT mines MUST be removed from the road entirely, either by carrying them off the road, or by destroying them with explosives. Merely using the \"disarm\" action then leaving them on the road is not enough!"\
  ""\
  ""\
  "<h2>MM trivia - how does this work?</h2>"\
  "Essentially, the road network is represented through a complex web of interdependent meta flags that form an undirected graph."\
  "Road junctions (not all, it's slightly simplified) are vertices, connecting roads are edges."\
  "Every vertex and edge is represented by a meta flag. A vertex flag is defined as true (i. e. reached) if all if any of its neighbor vertices is true, and the connecting edge flag is also true. The edge flag is true if that road segment is clear of obstacles and enemies."\
  "Vertices can have additional requirements, usually being clear of enemy forces and being physically visited by US forces."\
  "Whenever a flag is changed, the framework reevalutes all meta flags, which translates to a full graph traversal that checks whether the end vertex can be reached yet."
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 3
 }
 D2_Mission {
  coords 0 0 0
  m_sTitle "Mission"
  m_sTextData "<h2>II. MISSION</h2>"\
  ""\
  "Conduct route reconnaissance, identifying one viable route towards Nova Olesov."\
  "The route must be uninterrupted (roads/tracks only) and fully clear of obstacles."\
  ""\
  "<h2>III. EXECUTION</h2>"\
  ""\
  "Traverse the road network, locating and clearing removable obstacles and destroying enemy positions along the way."\
  "If a road is blocked by a major obstacle that cannot be quickly removed (e. g. abatis, vehicle barricade), an alternate route must be found."\
  "For this reason, it may be faster to first split the platoon into A/B sections on junctions."\
  "Desired end state is that the platoon has reached the eastern side of the AO, and there is some uninterrupted road without any obstacles leading up to it."\
  ""\
  "<h2>IV. ADMIN / LOGISTICS</h2>"\
  ""\
  "Alpha 3 includes a sapper who carries 5 explosive charges for destroying small obstacles like razor wire or mines. In addition, every LAV contains another 5 charges."\
  ""\
  "<h2>V. COMMAND / SIGNAL</h2>"\
  ""\
  "<b>Comsig:</b>"\
  "Alpha 1 (PL)"\
  "Alpha 2"\
  "Bravo 1 (PSG)"\
  "Bravo 2"
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 2
 }
 D0_Overview {
  coords 0 0 0
  m_sTitle "Overview"
  m_sTextData "1990s, Bystrany."\
  ""\
  "Yesterday, an MEU of the USMC started amphibious invasion of Bystrany. The goal is to reestablish the former government that was toppled by insurgent forces 2 weeks ago."\
  ""\
  "Over the course of the past day, the MEUs ground combat element was able to push about 3 kilometers inland, securing most major settlements and gaining a first solid foothold in the country."\
  ""\
  "The majority of enemy forces have retreated to the north east, with only smaller pockets remaining near the coast."\
  "The current goal of the enemy appears to be to delay the US main force, gaining time to reorganise and establish a more capable defensive posture further inland."\
  ""\
  "While Inland operations have so far been limited to small scale air assaults and infiltrations, the main force of the GCE next aims to seize the town of Nova Olesov."\
  ""\
  "To support that operation, your LAR platoon has been tasked with conducting a route reconnaissance east of Kamoryn, identifying viable supply routes towards Nova Olesov."
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
 }
}